WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.950
Welcome to our second drink of Chair Model.
欢迎收听我们的第二期“椅子模特”酒饮播客。

2
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.090
In this episode, we talk about the Scranton Business Park Five Families.
在本期节目中，我们聊到了斯克兰顿商务园的五大家族。

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.110
We got some fun behind-the-scenes tidbits from Paul Faust, who plays Cool Guy Paul.
我们从饰演酷哥保罗的保罗·浮士德那里听到了一些有趣的幕后花絮。

4
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:19.930
And of course, we discuss Michael's love for the chair model in the Office Supply magazine.
当然，我们还要讨论迈克尔对《办公用品》杂志上那个椅子模特的爱慕。

5
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.910
It's one of my favorite plot lines.
这是我最喜欢的剧情线之一。

6
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.510
I know, it's so perfect.
我知道，简直完美。

7
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.610
I'm going to kick us off with a fan theory that a lot of you wrote in about.
我先抛出一个很多观众来信提到的粉丝理论。

8
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.150
Douglas Kay and many others said,
道格拉斯·凯和许多其他人说：

9
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:35.970
I always thought the chair model looked like Jan, and that's why Michael was so obsessed with her.
我一直觉得这个椅子模特长得很像简，这就是为什么迈克尔对她如此痴迷。

10
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.250
And Asma wrote in and said,
阿斯玛来信说：

11
00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.350
The chair lady is Jan with black hair.
这位椅子女士就是留着黑发的简。

12
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.010
Jenna, what do you think about this theory?
珍娜，你觉得这个理论怎么样？

13
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.210
Should we look at a side-by-side?
我们要不要看看对比图？

14
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.830
You know I love a side-by-side.
你知道我最喜欢看对比图了。

15
00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:49.450
I know.
我知道。

16
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.430
I have it right here.
我这里正好有。

17
00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.070
I kind of, it's the eyes.
我觉得，主要是眼睛部分。

18
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.730
I see it a little bit.
我有一点看出来了。

19
00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.930
I see it in the eyes.
我在眼睛里看出来了。

20
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.070
Otherwise, I don't see it.
除此以外，我看不出来。

21
00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:04.490
If I'm being totally honest, Douglas and Asma, I'm sorry.
说句老实话，道格拉斯和阿斯玛，我很抱歉。

22
00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.910
I see it a little bit.
我确实看出来一点。

23
00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:06.850
I do.
真的看出来了。

24
00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.870
I can see why Michael, it looks like he has a type.
我能理解为什么迈克尔看起来像是对这种类型情有独钟。

25
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.630
I mean, his type is woman.
我是说，他的类型就是女的。

26
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:13.650
Truly.
确实。

27
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.710
Well, we also talked about the gal that Kevin is going to set Michael up with.
对了，我们还聊到了凯文要介绍给迈克尔的那个姑娘。

28
00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.010
You know, Wendy.
你知道的，温迪。

29
00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:26.070
But then Michael calls the phone number that Kevin gave him, and it's an actual Wendy's restaurant.
但后来迈克尔拨打了凯文给他的电话号码，结果打到了一家真正的温迪汉堡餐厅。

30
00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.070
I had reached out to Kent Svornak to find out who played Wendy, and he didn't remember.
我曾联系过肯·斯沃纳克想查出是谁演的温迪，但他不记得了。

31
00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:32.350
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

32
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:33.810
Corey L.
科里·L

33
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.310
wrote in to tell us that the voice of the Wendy's employee was played by Kelly Leskowitz.
来信告诉我们，温迪员工的声音是由凯利·莱斯科维茨配音的。

34
00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:45.110
And Corey included a link to Kelly's IMDb page, where it is listed among her many acting roles.
而且科里还附上了凯利IMDb主页的链接，上面列出了她众多演艺角色中的这一个。

35
00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:49.470
Well, Angela and I thought she crushed this moment, so I think we need to hear it.
嗯，安吉拉和我都觉得她这段演得太棒了，所以我觉得我们有必要听一下。

36
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:50.230
Okay.
好的。

37
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.090
Wendy.
温迪。

38
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.150
Hot and juicy redhead.
性感多汁的红发女郎。

39
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.210
Give this a try.
试试这个。

40
00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.510
Wendy's.
温迪汉堡。

41
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.710
Hello, Wendy.
喂，温迪。

42
00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.710
This is Kevin's friend, Michael.
我是凯文的朋友，迈克尔。

43
00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.930
This isn't Wendy.
这里不是温迪。

44
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.090
Oh, I'm sorry.
哦，不好意思。

45
00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:11.950
Could you put her on, please?
能让她接电话吗，拜托？

46
00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:14.050
Dude, this is a Wendy's restaurant.
老兄，这是温迪汉堡餐厅。

47
00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:17.550
Okay.
好吧。

48
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.360
Um, could I just have a frosty and a baked potato, please?
嗯，我能买一个冰淇淋和一个烤土豆吗，谢谢？

49
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.720
You have to come to the restaurant to order food.
你得来餐厅点餐。

50
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.980
Well, send somebody to pick it up.
那，派个人去取一下呗。

51
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:26.560
Just have it ready.
先准备好。

52
00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.600
It's ready now.
现在已经准备好了。

53
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.360
Well, put it aside.
好吧，先放一边。

54
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:34.250
Give her a read on, it's ready now.
让她试读一下，现在好了。

55
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.070
I love that line read.
我太喜欢那种台词念法了。

56
00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.870
I loved everything that she did in that moment.
我喜欢她在那个时刻做的所有事。

57
00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.130
I thought it was just so great.
我觉得真的太棒了。

58
00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.310
Well, Michael also goes on a cringy blind date with Pam's landlady,
迈克尔还和潘的房东进行了一次尴尬的相亲，

59
00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.510
and some folks wrote in asking us if this scene was a nod to the BBC office.
有些观众写信问我们，这个场景是不是在向英国版《办公室》致敬。

60
00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:54.750
You know, when David Brent attempts to go on a blind date with Susan in the Christmas special part two.
你知道的，就像圣诞特辑第二集中，大卫·布伦特试图和苏珊去相亲那样。

61
00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:55.830
Oh, I remember it.
哦，我想起来了。

62
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.690
It is also super cringy.
那个也超级尴尬。

63
00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.430
And you know what?
你知道吗？

64
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.450
I think they're right, because both scenes start out so similar.
我觉得他们说得对，因为这两个场景一开始太像了。

65
00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:06.710
One's at a cafe, one's at like a bar, but they start out very much on the same tone.
一个是咖啡馆，另一个有点像酒吧，但它们的开场基调非常相似。

66
00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:11.050
I'm going to play the first 36 seconds of this scene in the UK version,
我要播放英版中这个场景的前36秒，

67
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:14.370
and then we're going to play the first part of Michael's blind date.
然后我们要播放迈克尔相亲的前半段。

68
00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.790
Yeah, I spoke to her on the phone.
对，我在电话里和她聊过。

69
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.470
Seemed quite nice.
感觉人挺不错的。

70
00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.370
So, a bit of a stick, really.
所以，其实有点紧张。

71
00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:19.290
Not nerves.
不是紧张。

72
00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:20.890
Excitement, really.
其实是兴奋。

73
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.510
Not sexual, you know.
你知道的，不是那种性方面的。

74
00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.730
She says we're wearing a white chiffon scarf to help me spot her.
她说我们会戴一条白色雪纺围巾好让我认出她。

75
00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.870
So, um, oh, for fuck's sake.
所以，呃，靠，真他妈的。

76
00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:29.830
David?
大卫？

77
00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:30.910
Huh?
嗯？

78
00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.390
Yeah, hiya.
对，嗨。

79
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:33.990
Susan?
苏珊？

80
00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.070
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

81
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.210
Can I get you a drink?
要我给你买杯喝的吗？

82
00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:36.870
No, I'll get one.
不用，我自己买。

83
00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.350
Have you got one?
你有喝的吗？

84
00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.830
You go and sit down, I'll get one.
你先去坐吧，我去买。

85
00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.390
Our suspect has straight brown hair.
我们的嫌疑人留着直直的棕色头发。

86
00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.330
She is wearing blue jeans and a black top.
她穿着蓝色牛仔裤和黑色上衣。

87
00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.230
So, behold our bachelorette.
那么，来看看我们的单身女郎。

88
00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:55.250
Give her a 10 for looks and a 3 for her ability to describe herself.
外貌给10分，自我描述能力给3分。

89
00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.510
Hello, my lady?
你好，女士？

90
00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:03.570
Michael?
迈克尔？

91
00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:05.330
Huh?
嗯？

92
00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.610
Are you Michael Scott?
你是迈克尔·斯科特吗？

93
00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.970
Is who Michael what?
谁是迈克尔什么？

94
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.090
Oh, I'm sorry.
哦，对不起。

95
00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.130
I'm supposed to be meeting someone named Michael.
我本该见一个叫迈克尔的人。

96
00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.370
Oh, that's not, yeah.
哦，那不是，对。

97
00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:15.790
Michael?
迈克尔？

98
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:18.600
Michael?
迈克尔？

99
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.940
Large hot chocolate with caramel and a shot of peppermint.
大杯热巧克力加焦糖和一勺薄荷糖浆。

100
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.140
Okay, yes.
好的，是的。

101
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.000
I agree.
我同意。

102
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.040
It is, it's, yes.
就是，就是，对。

103
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:27.560
Right?
对吧？

104
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:27.980
Yeah.
对。

105
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:33.600
I think everyone that wrote in is right because basically they have a description of what this person might be wearing.
我觉得所有写信来的人都说得对，因为他们基本上都描述了这人可能穿着什么。

106
00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.140
Yep.
没错。

107
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.400
They're at a bar or cafe, like, looking around.
他们在一个酒吧或咖啡馆里，大概，四处张望。

108
00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.000
And then the person walks up and they're both like, oh, shit.
然后那个人走过来，他们俩都觉得，靠。

109
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:41.560
Yeah.
对。

110
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.080
Yeah.
对。

111
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.920
Have you ever been on a blind date?
你从来没约过盲约吗？

112
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.580
Like, truly, like, a blind date?
就是那种，真正的，盲约？

113
00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.000
No.
没有。

114
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.200
I haven't.
我没有。

115
00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:47.660
Have you?
你呢？

116
00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.160
No.
没有。

117
00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.120
I was never even, like, on a setup.
我甚至连，那种，被人安排相亲都没有过。

118
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.620
I've never even been set up.
我甚至从来没被人撮合过。

119
00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.860
No, I take that back.
不对，我收回刚才的话。

120
00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.320
I did get set up.
我确实被安排过一次。

121
00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.480
I was, like, I was invited to, like, a party.
我当时，就是，我被邀请去参加一个派对。

122
00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:57.920
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

123
00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.800
The sneaky setup.
偷偷摸摸的撮合。

124
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.340
But it was kind of known.
但其实大家都心知肚明。

125
00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.580
Actually, I don't think I did know.
其实，我觉得我当时并不知道。

126
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:12.200
I think once I got there, it became very clear to me that I had been invited as a potential love interest for, like, their single guy friend at the party because I was also single.
我觉得等我到了那儿，我才突然明白，我被邀请去是因为我是单身，派对上正好有个单身男青年，我是作为他的潜在发展对象被叫去的。

127
00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.420
This happened to me.
我也遇到过这种事。

128
00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.500
It's the sneaky setup.
这就是偷偷摸摸的撮合。

129
00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.220
It was my mom and a bunch of the church ladies.
是我妈和一群教堂的妇女搞的鬼。

130
00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.720
There was a new youth pastor.
来了一个新的青年牧师。

131
00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.460
They're trying to make a love connection happen.
她们千方百计想牵线搭桥。

132
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.120
Yeah.
对。

133
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.980
And it was so awkward.
而且尴尬得要死。

134
00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:30.760
It became very apparent to me that this whole gathering was so that the two of us might have a spark.
我很快就看出来了，这场聚会的全部目的就是为了让我们俩擦出点火花。

135
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.400
Same.
一样。

136
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.000
These people planned an entire game night.
这些人策划了一整场桌游之夜。

137
00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:34.300
Yeah.
对。

138
00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.140
We played running charades in hopes that I would have a connection with this guy.
我们玩了动态哑谜，就盼着我和这家伙能对上眼。

139
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:39.520
Yeah.
对。

140
00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.720
But I've never been on, like, just a one-on-one setup for a blind date.
但我从来没有经历过那种单独一对一的盲约。

141
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.420
No, me either.
没有，我也没有。

142
00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.380
My mom met my dad on a blind date.
我妈当年跟我爸就是相亲认识的。

143
00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.940
Oh, that's so romantic.
哦，太浪漫了。

144
00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:49.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

145
00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.560
When it goes right.
如果成功的话。

146
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:51.600
Yeah.
对。

147
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.380
It's a great story.
这是个很棒的故事。

148
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.800
Well, to wrap up, I went to the candy bag alts.
好了，总结一下，我去了糖果包的备选区。

149
00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:02.440
You guys know that there were talking heads from everyone as they wrote the names of women on index cards for Michael.
你们知道每个人在索引卡上为迈克尔写下女性名字时都有采访镜头吗。

150
00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.480
You know, Michael was like.
你们知道迈克尔当时那个反应吗。

151
00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.180
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

152
00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.620
You've got to all come up with names of people for me to date.
你们得都帮我想想可以和我约会的人名。

153
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:06.960
Yeah.
是啊。

154
00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.940
So there were a lot of these talking heads that didn't make it in.
所以有很多这样的访谈片段没能剪进去。

155
00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.900
People had strong reactions about writing these names on index cards.
大家对把这些名字写在索引卡片上反应强烈。

156
00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.600
I'm going to read you Toby and Oscar.
我要念给你们听的是托比和奥斯卡。

157
00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:16.060
Okay.
好的。

158
00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:22.420
Toby, forcing your employees to set you up isn't really a violation of any Dunder Mifflin rule,
托比，强迫你的员工给你牵线搭桥，其实并不算违反邓德米夫林的任何规定，

159
00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:27.120
mostly because nobody at corporate ever considered that someone would do this.
主要是因为公司总部从来没想过会有人这么做。

160
00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.440
Michael really thinks outside the box.
迈克尔真的很不走寻常路。

161
00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.220
Yeah, there's no rule because who would do that?
对啊，根本没有这条规定，因为谁会干这种事？

162
00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.140
Who would do that?
谁会干这种事？

163
00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.520
Here's Oscars.
这是奥斯卡的。

164
00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.260
Michael and my sister might hit it off.
迈克尔和我妹妹可能会很合得来。

165
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.060
Oh, Thanksgiving with Michael.
哦，和迈克尔一起过感恩节。

166
00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.720
You have to think ahead.
你得未雨绸缪。

167
00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.980
You got to plan ahead.
你得提前计划。

168
00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.540
All right, everybody.
好了，各位。

169
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:49.220
Please enjoy your second drink of Chair Model.
请享用你们的第二杯“椅子模特”。

170
00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.590
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

171
00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.890
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

172
00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.170
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

173
00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.410
And we're best friends.
而且我们是好朋友。

174
00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.250
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专为你们制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

175
00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.970
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

176
00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.230
that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有当时在场的两个人才能告诉你。

177
00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.370
We're The Office ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

178
00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:15.310
Hi, everybody.
大家好。

179
00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.330
Hello from our closets.
来自我们衣帽间的问候。

180
00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.690
Still here.
还在呢。

181
00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:22.910
Still in our closets.
依然在我们的衣帽间里。

182
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.550
Still surrounded by Josh's many, many hats.
周围依然环绕着乔什许许多多的帽子。

183
00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.230
So many baseball hats.
好多的棒球帽。

184
00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:28.930
So many.
真的好多。

185
00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.650
Does he have a favorite?
他有最喜欢的一顶吗？

186
00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.890
Can we get him on the pod to ask him to give us a breakdown of these hats?
我们能把他请上播客，让他给我们讲讲这些帽子吗？

187
00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.610
Are they significant emotionally in some way?
它们在某种程度上有特殊的感情意义吗？

188
00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:39.830
Do they represent a team he loves?
它们代表着他热爱的某支球队吗？

189
00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:43.150
I mean, no, I think Josh is all about the fit.
我是说，没有，我觉得乔什只看重版型。

190
00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:47.630
And it looks like he loves the Patagonia kind of trucker looking hat.
而且看起来他很喜欢巴塔哥尼亚那种卡车司机风格的帽子。

191
00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.950
It does with the adjustable band thing, the little plastic snappies.
确实，就是那种带调节带的，有小塑料按扣的。

192
00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.250
Josh, I hope you are excited that we shared.
乔什，希望你听到我们分享这些会感到兴奋。

193
00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.110
Listen, there's other things in the closet.
听着，衣帽间里还有别的东西。

194
00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.970
Right over my shoulder, I notice all the time that there's the,
就在我肩膀上方，我老是注意到那个，

195
00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.630
what's the stuff they spray in their shoes, Jenna?
那是他们喷在鞋子里的东西叫什么来着，珍娜？

196
00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:05.610
Febreze?
织物清新剂？

197
00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:06.450
No.
不对。

198
00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:08.690
All dudes do this.
所有老兄都这样。

199
00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.510
They spray that stuff in their shoes.
他们把那玩意儿喷在鞋子里。

200
00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:11.390
Odor eaters?
鞋用除臭剂？

201
00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.550
Yes, yes.
好啦，好啦。

202
00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.130
Anyway.
言归正传。

203
00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.590
Oh, now, Josh, you're really happy.
哦，现在，乔什，你可真高兴啊。

204
00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:17.150
I've shared with everyone that you spray your shoes.
我已经跟所有人都说过你往鞋子上喷除臭剂了。

205
00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.850
Well, because we need to talk about this longer,
好吧，因为我们需要多聊会儿这个，

206
00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:28.590
I am really curious about the very bright red pair of shoes over your shoulder in the shoe cubby.
我对你肩膀后面鞋架上那双亮红色的鞋子非常好奇。

207
00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:29.710
Whose are those?
那是谁的？

208
00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.790
Oh, those are my red Converse.
哦，那是我的红色匡威。

209
00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:32.950
Okay, so here's the thing.
好啦，情况是这样的。

210
00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:37.550
Yes, this is Josh's closet, but I occupy most of the shoe space.
没错，这是乔什的衣橱，不过鞋柜的大部分空间都被我占了。

211
00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:39.750
I have lots of shoes.
我有很多鞋子。

212
00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.090
You have overflow that goes into his closet.
你的鞋多得都溢出来，占到他的衣橱里去了。

213
00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:43.710
Yeah, he's real happy about it.
对啊，他可高兴了呢。

214
00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:48.130
Well, guys, it's what you're here for, a breakdown of Angela's closet.
好了，各位，这就是你们今天来这的目的——盘点安吉拉的衣橱。

215
00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.570
Next week, we'll do my closet.
下周，我们要盘点我的衣橱。

216
00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.970
But this week, we are talking about chair model.
但本周，我们要聊的是“椅子模特”。

217
00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.190
It's so good.
这集太棒了。

218
00:08:55.630 --> 00:09:01.010
Season four, episode 14, written by BJ Novak, directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
第四季第14集，BJ·诺瓦克编剧，杰弗里·布里茨导演。

219
00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.830
With a duo like that, you know it's going to be good.
有了这样的黄金搭档，你知道这集肯定错不了。

220
00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:10.430
I love the simple idea that Michael has a thing for the model in a chair catalog.
我特别喜欢这个简单的设定：迈克尔迷上了椅子目录里的一个模特。

221
00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.250
I just love how simple and perfect that is.
我就是觉得这个设定既简单又完美。

222
00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:13.910
Yes.
没错。

223
00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.570
Let me give you a summary.
我来给大家总结一下剧情。

224
00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:16.410
Do it.
讲吧。

225
00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.850
Michael is unable to pick a new chair for his office
迈克尔无法为办公室挑选新椅子，

226
00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:25.130
after he becomes infatuated with a woman modeling office chairs in a catalog.
因为他迷恋上了一个在目录里展示办公椅的女性。

227
00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.750
He decides he's ready to rejoin the dating pool.
他决定重返约会市场。

228
00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:31.790
He's inspired by his love of the chair model.
他受到了对椅子模特爱慕之情的启发。

229
00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:39.570
Meanwhile, the Dunder Mifflin parking spaces are being used by a construction crew doing work
与此同时，邓德·米夫林的停车位被一家建筑施工队占用了，

230
00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.530
for W.B.
他们在为W.B.

231
00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:41.210
Jones.
琼斯公司施工。

232
00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:45.110
And the staff of Dunder Mifflin has to park in a satellite lot.
邓德·米夫林的员工不得不把车停在远处的临时停车场。

233
00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:50.290
Kevin and Andy join forces to confront the other bosses of the Scranton Business Park
凯文和安迪联手去质问斯克兰顿商业园的其他老板，

234
00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.670
to reclaim their places in the main lot.
以夺回他们在主停车场的车位。

235
00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.450
Simple storylines.
简单的故事情节。

236
00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.790
Absolute perfection.
简直完美。

237
00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:58.950
Also, absolutely true.
而且，完全真实。

238
00:09:59.270 --> 00:09:59.610
Yeah.
是啊。

239
00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:04.430
You know, I had to park in a satellite lot when I had my admin job.
你知道的，我以前做行政工作时，也得停在远处的停车场。

240
00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:09.450
If you were an executive, you could park in the parking lot of the building,
如果你是高管，你就能把车停在大楼的停车场里，

241
00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:11.990
this high rise in downtown Los Angeles.
那是一栋位于洛杉矶市中心的高层建筑。

242
00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:12.670
Yeah.
对。

243
00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.750
I did not get a parking space.
我可没有停车位。

244
00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:19.530
I had to park in a satellite lot that was about a half a mile away.
我得把车停在大概半英里外的临时停车场。

245
00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.770
And it wasn't a big deal, except for on days that it rained.
这倒没什么大不了的，除了下雨天。

246
00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:23.910
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，情况是这样的。

247
00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.670
You know where you rank in a company by where you park.
从你停车的位置就能看出你在公司里的级别。

248
00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:27.530
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

249
00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:29.670
Well, Michael has a spot right up front.
迈克尔可有个最正前方的车位呢。

250
00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.710
He's not concerned.
他可一点儿也不操心。

251
00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:35.650
Well, later, he's going to try to imagine what it would be like if he didn't have that spot.
好吧，待会儿，他会试着想象如果他没有那个车位会是什么样子。

252
00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:36.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

253
00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:41.690
But it takes two employees angrily confronting him for him to get there.
但必须经过两名员工愤怒地与他当面对质，他才肯罢休。

254
00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.190
What are our fast facts, Jenna?
珍娜，我们的快速事实有哪些？

255
00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:51.250
Fast fact number one, the original title of this episode was Michael Dating.
快速事实一，本集的最初标题是《迈克尔约会》。

256
00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.230
Hmm.
嗯。

257
00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:59.690
But they realized that they would have to release the name of the episode before Dinner Party had aired.
但他们意识到，他们必须在《晚宴派对》播出之前就公布这集的剧名。

258
00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.710
Oh, and they didn't want that.
哦，他们不想那样。

259
00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:05.110
They didn't want to ruin the surprise about Jan and Michael's breakup, right?
他们不想剧透简和迈克尔分手的事情，对吧？

260
00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.010
Yes.
是的。

261
00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.050
So they changed the name of the episode to Parking.
所以他们把这集的标题改成了《停车位》。

262
00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:15.250
But then they felt, well, while it's a big part of the episode, it's not the main storyline of the episode.
但后来他们觉得，虽然这占了很大一部分，但并不是这一集的主要剧情。

263
00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.670
So they eventually settled on Chair Model, which I personally love.
所以他们最终选定了《椅子模特》，我个人非常喜欢这个名字。

264
00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:23.890
I mean, when you see that, aren't you intrigued?
我是说，当你看到这个时，难道不会觉得好奇吗？

265
00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:25.170
I'm so intrigued.
我太好奇了。

266
00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.210
What is this episode going to be about?
这一集到底会讲什么？

267
00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:28.090
Chair Model.
《椅子模特》。

268
00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.870
I'm more intrigued than Parking.
比起《停车位》，我对这个更感兴趣。

269
00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:30.470
I'll say that.
我敢这么说。

270
00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.050
They picked the right one.
他们选对了。

271
00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:32.830
All right.
好吧。

272
00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:39.010
Fast fact number two, I think we need to do a little breakdown of the Scranton Business Park Five Families.
快速事实二，我觉得我们需要稍微剖析一下斯克兰顿商业园的五大家族。

273
00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.190
I mean, it's like Goodfellas.
我是说，这就像《好家伙》一样。

274
00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:42.230
It is.
确实如此。

275
00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:43.690
All right.
好吧。

276
00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.930
Here are the bosses of the five families.
以下是五大家族的老大。

277
00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.710
Michael Scott, of course.
当然是迈克尔·斯科特。

278
00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.010
Bob Vance, Vance Refrigeration.
鲍勃·万斯，万斯冷冻公司。

279
00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.950
Then there is W.B.
然后是W.B.

280
00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.590
Jones from W.B.
琼斯，来自W.B.

281
00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:54.530
Jones Heating and Air.
琼斯冷暖设备公司。

282
00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.690
He was played by Barry Sigismundi.
他由巴里·西吉斯蒙迪饰演。

283
00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:02.030
Bill Kress of Kress, Tool & Die, who was played by Terrence Beeser.
克雷斯模具五金公司的比尔·克雷斯，由特伦斯·比瑟饰演。

284
00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:10.570
And finally, Paul Faust of Disaster Kits Limited, who was played by Paul FauSt.
最后是灾难应急包有限公司的保罗·浮士德，由保罗·浮士德本人饰演。

285
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:20.210
This is an amazing story, and it all starts when an actual man named Paul Faust came to visit the set of The Office.
这是一个神奇的故事，这一切都始于一个名叫保罗·浮士德的真实人物去《办公室》剧组探班。

286
00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.310
Yes.
是的。

287
00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.630
So I have known Paul Faust for years.
我和保罗·浮士德认识好多年了。

288
00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:28.790
We used to be related by marriage, and I reached out to him, and he is just such a hoot.
我们曾经是亲戚，我联系了他，他真的是个妙人。

289
00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:33.330
And he sent in all of these fantastic audio clips about his day on set.
他发来了所有这些关于他片场一天的精彩音频剪辑。

290
00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:34.850
But they are amazing.
它们真的太棒了。

291
00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:40.070
And in this first one, he explains exactly how he got the role on the show.
在第一段音频中，他详细解释了他是如何得到剧中角色的。

292
00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.110
Sam, you've got to play this clip.
萨姆，你得放一下这段音频。

293
00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.670
Hey, office ladies and office fans.
嘿，办公室女士们和办公室粉丝们。

294
00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:47.450
This is Paul Faust, a.k.a.
我是保罗·浮士德，也就是

295
00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.350
Cool Guy Paul.
酷哥保罗。

296
00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:50.290
I want to tell you how I got a part of the show.
我想告诉大家我是怎么得到这个角色的。

297
00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.610
So I was out in L.A.
当时我在洛杉矶

298
00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:57.310
on business and decided to visit the set because my cousins are part of the office.
出差，决定去片场参观，因为我的表亲们是《办公室》剧组的人。

299
00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:03.650
And when I was out there, I met the writers, and I kind of told them one of my companies what I did, which was a company that sells disaster kits.
当我在那儿的时候，我遇到了编剧们，我顺便跟他们提到了我的一家公司以及我的业务，那是一家销售灾难应急包的公司。

300
00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:05.970
And Greg had said, this is my cousin.
格雷格曾说过，这是我的表亲。

301
00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.250
He's a little nuts.
他有点神经质。

302
00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:07.970
Tell him what you do.
告诉他你是做什么的。

303
00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:09.370
I told him about the company.
我跟他说过这家公司的事。

304
00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.870
And when I walked out of the room, unbeknownst to me, B.J.
然后当我走出房间时，在我不知情的情况下，B.J.

305
00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:17.150
Novak said, that guy's got to be a character on the show.
诺瓦克说，这家伙一定要成为剧里的一个角色。

306
00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.810
So he wrote a part based on me.
所以他以我为原型写了一个角色。

307
00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:24.490
And the day before they shot the scene, they hadn't found an actor to play the part.
就在他们拍摄这场戏的前一天，他们还没找到演员来演这个角色。

308
00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:28.570
So I got a call asking me if I wanted to audition to play the part.
所以我接到一个电话，问我愿不愿意去试镜演这个角色。

309
00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:35.110
And long story short, I got the part, got to fly out and be part of the awesome show and play myself.
简而言之，我得到了这个角色，得以飞过去参与这部超棒的剧并饰演我自己。

310
00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:38.010
So that's how I got to be on the show.
这就是我如何加入这部剧的。

311
00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:40.350
It's really a story only can happen in Hollywood.
这真的是一个只会发生在好莱坞的故事。

312
00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.330
I mean, that's bonkers.
我是说，这太疯狂了。

313
00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.370
I know.
我知道。

314
00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.970
He's literally playing himself.
他简直是在演他自己。

315
00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.630
But what's bonkers to me about it was that they did hold auditions.
但我觉得最疯狂的是，他们居然真的举行了试镜。

316
00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.870
They held auditions for this role.
他们为这个角色举行了试镜。

317
00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:56.730
And the night before, they just had not found someone who could play Paul FauSt.
而在前一天晚上，他们居然还没找到能演保罗·浮士德的人。

318
00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.650
So they're like, how about Paul Faust?
所以他们就在想，保罗·浮士德怎么样？

319
00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:01.010
Paul really sells disaster kits.
保罗真的是卖灾难应急包的。

320
00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.090
That's real.
那是真的。

321
00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:03.630
That is his company.
那确实是他的公司。

322
00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:04.550
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

323
00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:07.230
And Angela, he talked about that in this next clip.
安吉拉，他在接下来的这段视频里也谈到了这一点。

324
00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:12.610
I think one of the most unique things about me being in the office was that I actually played myself.
我觉得我能参演《办公室》最独特的地方之一，就是我其实演的是我自己。

325
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.830
When I went out to L.A.
当我去了洛杉矶

326
00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:20.650
and I was visiting and I went to the set, I talked about one of the businesses I run, which is a company called 1-800-PREPARE.
去参观并来到片场时，我谈到了我经营的一项业务，那是一家叫做1-800-PREPARE的公司。

327
00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:26.010
1-800-PREPARE.com, where we actually sell disaster kits and preparedness kits.
1-800-PREPARE.com，我们真正在那里销售灾难应急包和备灾包。

328
00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.270
So I talked about it.
所以我谈到了这个。

329
00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:30.190
And that's what DJ had picked up on.
这就是DJ注意到的地方。

330
00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:34.910
And so he wrote a part called about Cool Guy Paul, the owner of Disaster Kits Limited.
于是他写了一个关于炫酷男保罗的角色，也就是灾难应急包有限公司的老板。

331
00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.930
And yes, I still own that company.
是的，我依然拥有那家公司。

332
00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:39.510
We still sell disaster kits.
我们仍在销售灾难应急包。

333
00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:48.570
So I think I'm one of the few people who played himself on TV with his real name in a real business that he runs, which was kind of cool.
所以我认为我是为数不多能在电视上用真名、经营着自己的真实生意并饰演自己的人之一，这感觉挺酷的。

334
00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:54.090
So we asked Paul, how did he prepare, you know, to have these scenes?
所以我们问保罗，你知道的，他是如何为这些戏份做准备的？

335
00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.130
He's not an actor.
他不是演员。

336
00:14:55.310 --> 00:15:01.170
He's not used to learning lines or where to sit, you know, how to navigate a set and all that kind of stuff.
他不习惯背台词，不知道该坐在哪里，你知道的，不知道怎么在片场走位以及诸如此类的事情。

337
00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.370
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

338
00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.010
So I got this part, let's say, on a Thursday.
所以我拿到这个角色，比方说是在周四。

339
00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.490
And I had we were shooting Friday morning.
我们周五早上就要拍摄。

340
00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.530
So I had about a good 10 hours to learn my five or six lines.
所以我大概有整整10个小时来记住我的五六句台词。

341
00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:14.890
So I'm studying, studying on the plane.
所以我一直在飞机上学啊学。

342
00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:15.570
I'm reading them.
我一直在读它们。

343
00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:16.470
I didn't sleep.
我没睡觉。

344
00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.130
I studied them.
我一直在背它们。

345
00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:21.750
So we go there and this whole experience happens and you're nervous and there's a lot of people around.
所以我们去了那里，整个经历发生了，你会感到紧张，周围有很多人。

346
00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.950
And I had 10 hours to learn a bunch of lines.
我只有10个小时来背一堆台词。

347
00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:25.970
So I was able to do it.
所以我还是做到了。

348
00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.470
And we knocked it out and I got it done.
我们顺利完成了，我搞定了。

349
00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:29.750
And I was like, great, I finished.
当时我想，太好了，我完成了。

350
00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:34.410
And then all of a sudden, somebody came in and they threw these new scripts down.
然后突然之间，有人走进来，把这些新剧本扔了下来。

351
00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.130
They said, OK, here's the alternate ending.
他们说，好，这是备用结局。

352
00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:39.230
Let's take a five minute break, learn our lines and come back to you.
我们休息五分钟，背一下台词再回来找你。

353
00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.070
And I'm like, wait, wait, what a minute?
当时我的反应是，等等，等等，什么情况？

354
00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.010
Five minutes, what?
五分钟，什么？

355
00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.110
I had 10 hours to learn my lines.
我原本有10个小时来背台词。

356
00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.350
Five minutes, I'm not learning new lines.
五分钟，我可背不出新台词。

357
00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:51.970
So I raced out the hallway, had to study, learn all the lines, learn when I came in and whatever.
所以我冲到走廊外，抓紧时间学习，背下所有的台词，搞清楚什么时候出场之类的事情。

358
00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.450
I wound up doing it, knocking it out, getting it done right.
我最后还是完成了，顺利拿下，搞定了。

359
00:15:56.130 --> 00:16:00.970
And again, life experience with amazing people who were just so supportive.
而且再说一次，这段人生经历遇到了那么多棒极了、给予我巨大支持的人。

360
00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.590
And I was glad that I was able to be a tiny part of this amazing family.
我也很高兴自己能成为这个温馨大家庭里微不足道的一部分。

361
00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:10.390
Well, Angela, I found an interview with Paul and he said that he landed in L.A.
安吉拉，我找到了一段保罗的采访，他说他凌晨1点30分落地洛杉矶。

362
00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.030
at 1.30 in the morning.
航空公司弄丢了他的行李。

363
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.770
The airline lost his luggage.
所以他没有行李。

364
00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.010
So he had no luggage.
他到达酒店，大约凌晨3点15分才睡下，结果早上5点就得起床

365
00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:22.910
He got to his hotel and went to sleep about 3.15 in the morning and he had to be up at 5 a.m.
去工作。

366
00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:23.530
for work.
经历这一切之后，我真的很震惊。

367
00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:27.270
So after all of that, I'm kind of amazed.
我要是遇到这情况肯定神志不清了。

368
00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.730
I would have been loopy.
我绝对没法背新台词。

369
00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.570
I wouldn't have been able to learn new lines.
完全不行。

370
00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:31.390
No.
而且我想象着保罗当时根本没睡。

371
00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:35.230
And I think of Paul just like he's had no sleep.
他大概穿着同一条内衣，因为行李丢了。

372
00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:39.190
He's probably in the same underwear because they lost his bag.
而且，你懂的，他本来以为已经到了终点线，结果他们又给他派发了全新任务。

373
00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:46.570
And he, you know, and now he's like, he thought he reached the finish line and then they hand him this whole new task.
保罗发来了一些关于他片场经历的更多小片段。

374
00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:51.110
Well, Paul sent a few more clips about his experience just being on set.
它们太逗了。

375
00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:51.970
They're so delightful.
我们会在这一期的节目中穿插播放这些内容。

376
00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.110
We're going to sprinkle those in throughout the episode.
好的。

377
00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:55.030
All right.
第三个快速冷知识，安吉拉。

378
00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:56.850
Fast fact number three, Angela.
嗯哼。

379
00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:57.550
Mm-hmm.
我给这个板块起名叫：我是这一集的灵感来源吗？

380
00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:01.950
I'm titling this, Am I the Inspiration for This Episode?
不好意思，你说什么？

381
00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.030
I'm sorry, what?
你演过椅子模特吗？

382
00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.130
Were you a chair model?
没有，但是在剧集第一季的时候，我想要前台换一把新椅子，我还为此去争取过。

383
00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:15.770
No, but in season one of the show, I wanted a new chair at reception and I had to lobby for it.
所以我确信我不是这一集的灵感来源，但在第一季里，他们给我配了一把没有扶手的椅子。

384
00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:24.410
So I'm sure I'm not the inspiration for this episode, but in season one, they gave me a chair at reception without arMs.
那是一把无扶手的椅子。

385
00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.150
It was an armless chair.
但我真的、真的很想要一把带扶手的椅子。

386
00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.310
And I really, really wanted a chair with arMs.
于是我尝试着去挪椅子，或者找一把可能没人认领也没人用的椅子。

387
00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:36.850
And so I attempted to try to sort of move the chairs or find a chair maybe that hadn't been claimed or used.
根本行不通。

388
00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.190
It wasn't working.
非常感谢我们的布景师史蒂夫·罗斯斯坦，因为他是负责挑选《办公室》所有家具的团队负责人之一。

389
00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:46.070
And big shout out to our set dresser, Steve Rothstein, because he is one of the guys who headed up the team that picked out all our furniture on the office.
是他帮我弄到了一把带扶手的椅子。

390
00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.170
And he got me a chair with arMs.
哦，天哪。

391
00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:49.330
Oh, lady.
当时我太兴奋了。

392
00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.930
And I was so excited.
好吧，我也有一个关于椅子的故事要告诉你。

393
00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:53.270
Well, I have a chair story for you.
我一直憋着没说呢。

394
00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.070
I've been holding on to this.
我干脆现在就告诉你吧。

395
00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:57.190
I'm going to go ahead and tell you now.
我现在坐的这把椅子。

396
00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.350
The chair I'm sitting in right now.
准备好了吗？

397
00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:00.090
Ready?
我要把镜头摇下去了。

398
00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.270
I'm going to pan down.
看到这把椅子了吗？

399
00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:02.630
Do you see this chair?
看到了。

400
00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:03.730
I do.
我看到了。

401
00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.910
It's a blue chair with mesh.
这是一把带网眼材质的蓝色椅子。

402
00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.630
Do you recognize it?
你认得它吗？

403
00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:10.630
I don't recognize it, but it has no arMs.
我不认识，但它没有扶手。

404
00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:12.950
Phil Shea gave me this chair.
菲尔·希a送了我这把椅子。

405
00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.990
It was a leftover chair from Workbus.
这是《工作巴士》剩下的椅子。

406
00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.870
Oh, my gosh.
噢，我的天啊。

407
00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.050
You've been sitting in a Workbus chair this whole time.
你这段时间一直坐着一把《工作巴士》的椅子。

408
00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:32.970
For a year in my closet, I have been sitting in my Workbus chair, and I was going to save it for Workbus, but we're having all this chair talk.
我把我的《工作巴士》椅子藏在衣柜里整整一年，本来想留着等《工作巴士》开拍再用，但我们聊了这么多关于椅子的事。

409
00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.330
I couldn't hold it in anymore.
我再也憋不住了。

410
00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:43.210
Well, I just have to say this is why our show is so great, because getting a chair is a very relatable big deal moment.
好吧，我只想说这就是我们节目这么棒的原因，因为搞到一把椅子是一个特有共鸣的大事件。

411
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:51.550
When you are in an office job or any job, your chair, you sit in it all day, and they created this amazing, wonderful storyline out of it.
当你在做办公室工作或任何工作时，你的椅子，你一整天都坐在上面，他们竟然能从中延伸出一个精彩、美妙的故事线。

412
00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:56.110
Yes, and thank you, Phil Shea, because I had gotten a desk.
是的，谢谢菲尔·希a，因为我之前弄到了一张书桌。

413
00:18:56.310 --> 00:19:01.730
You know, I had in the corner of my guest room a little desk where I would sit and do work, and I didn't have a proper desk chair.
你知道的，我客房的角落里有一张小桌子，我通常会在那里坐着办公，但我没有一张合适的办公椅。

414
00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:06.330
I was using one of the kitchen chairs, and I was sort of talking about it on set, and Phil Shea was like,
我一直用的是厨房的椅子，我当时在片场随口提了一下，菲尔·希a就说，

415
00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:08.530
Ange, I have some extra chairs from Workbus.
安琪，我这有一些《工作巴士》的多余椅子。

416
00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:09.430
Do you want one?
你想要一把吗？

417
00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:10.810
I was like, yes!
我当时就说，要！

418
00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.530
This is making me happy.
这让我感到很高兴。

419
00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.390
I know.
我知道。

420
00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:14.930
We all have a chair story.
我们每个人都有一段关于椅子的故事。

421
00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:20.770
And I have been sitting in it for a year with you and haven't told you, because I was going to try to work it in a Workbus.
而且我和你一起坐了它一年都没告诉你，因为我本来想试着把它弄进《工作巴士》里。

422
00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.070
But there you go.
但事情就是这样。

423
00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:25.590
Let's take a break, and when we get back, we'll get into it.
我们先休息一下，等回来后，我们就开始深入探讨。

424
00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:26.370
All right.
好的。

425
00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:37.390
We are back.
我们回来了。

426
00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:40.630
We open on a Jim and Pam talking head.
镜头开始于吉姆和帕姆的单人采访画面。

427
00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:47.350
They are standing outside of the Dunder Mifflin office, and they are explaining that due to some renovations in the building,
他们站在邓德米夫林办公室外面，解释说由于大楼正在进行一些装修，

428
00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:54.310
all of their parking spots are being taken up, and they have to park in a satellite lot and walk to work.
他们所有的停车位都被占用了，他们不得不把车停在远处的临时停车场，然后步行去上班。

429
00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.690
They're being really positive about it, though.
不过他们对此真的很乐观。

430
00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:01.010
Yeah, they saw a junkyard dog eating, you know, some of a chicken.
对，他们看到一只废品场的狗在吃，你知道的，吃一点鸡肉。

431
00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:06.890
Yeah, eating the bones of a rotisserie chicken, Angela, which was based on a real story.
对，在吃烤鸡的骨头，安琪，这可是基于真实的故事改编的。

432
00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.450
Yeah, it was.
对，确实是。

433
00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:19.910
There was a junkyard next to our real office building, and there was a junkyard dog who they would throw like old rotisserie chicken bones to.
我们真正的办公大楼旁边有一个废品场，那里有一只废品场的狗，大家会把吃剩的烤鸡骨头之类的东西扔给它吃。

434
00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.770
We've talked about this junkyard and the dog.
我们聊过这个废品场和这只狗。

435
00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:26.070
We got very invested in this dog's life that lived over there.
我们对住在那边的那只狗的生活投入了很深的感情。

436
00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:26.850
We did.
我们确实如此。

437
00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.730
And it made it into an episode.
而且它还被写进了一集里。

438
00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:37.670
So then we have Oscar and Andy, who are less positive, and then there's Kevin, who is just downright angry.
然后我们有奥斯卡和安迪，他们没那么乐观，接着还有凯文，他简直气坏了。

439
00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:41.810
Kevin is going to have a breakdown over this satellite parking lot.
凯文要为这个远端停车场崩溃了。

440
00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:42.370
Yeah.
对。

441
00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:47.270
Well, Andy says he's so bummed because he lost a penny out of his penny loafers.
好吧，安迪说他很难过，因为他的便士乐福鞋上掉了一枚硬币。

442
00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:48.030
Yeah.
对。

443
00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.250
Jenna, I don't understand penny loafers, so I looked them up.
珍娜，我不懂便士乐福鞋，所以我去查了一下。

444
00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:51.990
Oh.
哦。

445
00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:53.470
You could have asked me.
你本可以问我的。

446
00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:56.850
I wore penny loafers all through high school as part of my school uniform.
我整个高中时期都穿着便士乐福鞋，作为校服的一部分。

447
00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:59.810
Okay, well, why did you put a penny in your penny loafer?
好吧，那你为什么要在便士乐福鞋里放一枚硬币呢？

448
00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:03.230
I don't know, because there was a slot there for it.
我不知道，因为那里刚好有个卡槽。

449
00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:04.650
Okay, well, I'll tell you.
好吧，那我来告诉你。

450
00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:05.830
I'll tell you why.
我来告诉你为什么。

451
00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:07.550
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

452
